In my experience, they're for specifying an option that doesn't seem to 
actually do anything. :-)

I've run across plenty of read errors on a variety of drives that for 
whatever reason weren't remapped automatically and had to be done 
manually.  Many of them didn't appear to be soft errors, either, since 
even huge numbers of retries failed to pick them up again.  I've had 
this happen on lots of 4 gig Seagate Medalist drives.  I don't have one 
handy to check its mode page settings.  I do have a Quantum Fireball SE 
8.4 gig online right now, though, and despite the fact that it has those 
mode page parameters turned on, I know I had one of those drives fail to 
remap a hard error last year.

Maybe all the drives I use just have buggy firmware, but whatever the 
reason, I've done enough manual remaps not to trust it.

