A couple of weeks ago, I posted a query to this group asking if Travan 4
tape drives would work under DU 4.0. Although I didn't get any replies, I
thought I'd report that I've tried it for myself and it works fine, albeit
with a couple of provisos:

	1. you need to explicitly specify the tape blocking factor 
	   (using the 'b' option) when using tar or restore to read a
	   tape, as the automatic block size detection doesn't appear to
	   handle Travan drives

	2. you can't append to an existing tar archive on the tape (the 
	   tar -r option)


Other than that, it works fine for what I want to do (getting old user
accounts off the disks) although the back-up speed as measured by tapex is
only a little over 30 MB/min (against the 72 MB/min claimed for the
drive).

Andy




