Here's some Solaris/Tru64 NFS behaviour that I don't understand. We have
a filesystem on a Alphaserver running Tru64 v5.0A that is automounted on
a Sun system running Solaris 7 (32-bit). On the Sun, I try to use gzip to
compress a file on the (auto)mounted Alphaserver disk...

  sun% gzip afile
  afile.gz: Value too large for defined data type

  sun% ls -l afile*
  afile.gz: Value too large for defined data type
  -rw-rw-r--   1 user  group   37006 Sep 21 21:10 afile

Now, here's the view of the same fileystem on the Alphaserver..

   alpha% ls -l afile*
  -rw-rw-r--   1 user  group   37006 Sep 21 21:10 afile
  ----------   1 user  group       0 Mar 24  1964 afile.gz

Note the date on the zero-length afile.gz file. What's going on here?
Is this a 32/64-bit problem, an NFSv2/v3 problem, or what?

