srlnrow@read.the.sig writes:

>Now, here's the view of the same fileystem on the Alphaserver..

>   alpha% ls -l afile*
>  -rw-rw-r--   1 user  group   37006 Sep 21 21:10 afile
>  ----------   1 user  group       0 Mar 24  1964 afile.gz

The negative (1964) timestamp cannot be represented over
NFS.  Typically, these were send over the wire unconverted
but Solaris 7 no longer accepts them.

If you can, use SOlaris 8 and set nfs_allow_preepoch_time to 1.

>Note the date on the zero-length afile.gz file. What's going on here?
>Is this a 32/64-bit problem, an NFSv2/v3 problem, or what?


Look at how the file is created; trace the NFS packets.

It shouldn't have a negative timestamp.

Casper
