After reading Eric's message I just did the forehead slap.  Your
disk-buffer settings are probably way too high, and the
swap-space-forecasting algorithm is probably taking them into account.
So in addition to what I recommended in .1, please drop your UBC
parameters and the AdvFS cache size as well, as appropriate for your
filesystem types, system size, and workload.  The tuning guide will have
descriptions of all the settings.

Don't "shotgun" the UBC settings.  They need to be adjusted as a group
so they maintain a specific relationship to each other.  A common
mistake is to drop ubc_maxpercent way down and fail to adjust downward,
in a relative fashion, the other UBC params.  I have seen this throw a
monkey wrench into the gears of the VM subsystem, so watch out.

Apologies for having forgotten to mention this before, and thanks to
Eric for jogging my memory.

If you want to describe your system and your workload and place the
output of sys_check (run while the system is under its maximum usual
load) in this thread, I'll give you some reasonable values for the above
params.  At least it'll give you a starting point.

Sys_check is available at
