Actually vdump and vrestore were modified to back up UFS.
Normally the -D option is used on ufs to specify the directory.

The easiest method is to boot from CD.
Mount the old root on /mnt
Mount the new root on /mnt2
vdump -0f - -D /mnt |vrestore -xf - -D /mnt2
change /etc/fstab according and reboot.

(I would recommend migrating to advfs, but then thats just my humble
opinion)

hth
