You may not need to.  Use the "collect/collgui" tool to monitor your
long-term memory usage.  If your swap usage remains consistently low,
you can probably get by with lazy swap (you are probably running
immediate swap now).  See the swapon man page.

In the V4 stream you make the change by removing a soft link.  In the V5
stream you make a 1-line change in sysconfigtab.  The man page for your
O.S. will explain it, along with the benefits and caveats of each
method.  It's a piece o' cake to change.

The reason for the messages, by the way, is not to let you know that the
O.S is running short on swap but rather to alert you to the fact that it
can't GUARANTEE you'll have all the swap space you MIGHT need based on
the current configuration.

On all my test systems I run lazy swap and run memory usage right up to
within about 4K pages of memory exhaustion with no ill effects, FWIW.
That's on V5.

Good luck,
WJD


