Hi Maarten,

I don;t have any specs on GB Ethernet from Tru64 but I have some results
with Cisco equipment (swicth to switch and switch to router) but the speeds
leave alot to be desired! The maximum speeds that you can get are about
350Mb/s Not very strange since the transimission is still done over a 100MHz
signal. The transmissions are spead up by phase modulation and signal
optimizing. SO it is not a true 1000MHz signal. Not strange either since the
higher the frequency the smaller the distance. When one would be able to get
a 1000MHz signal through a standard copper wire (longer than 1 or 2 meters)
then you would still lose all the signal once you make a curve in the wire.
The signal will try to go straight ahead and radiate out form the corner and
everything is lost.

So don't expect a miracle from 1Gb/s networking, eventhough 300Mb/s is very
nice over standard copper wiring.

Raymond

