Hello Helmut,

On Tue, 5 Sep 2000, Helmut Michels wrote:
> ... tries to login
> into a NIS client or into the NIS slave, he gets the error
>  "Can't rewrite protected password entry for user ....', and the login
> is rejected.  Version 4.0F of Compaq Tru64 is installed on the NIS
> master
> and on the NIS slave.

Not having experiences with Trunix 4.0F/C2 ... but following the
manuals for V5.0A there are two features strict C2 would require but
which are recommended to change for better login performance by Compaq.
Every login time the tty and the time will tried to be recorded as
a direct modification of the NIS masters prpasswd following a make/push.
This behaviour is controlled by the systems' default template.
Setting up "d_skip_success_login_log:" and "d_skip_ttys_update:"
with "edauth -dd default" on all machines (both NIS (slave) servers and
clients) should prevent this, thus not requiring a running NIS master
at login time or rare situations - provided the slaves are in the 
ypservers map.)

Hoping these things are true for V4.0F, too.

Please see also:

http://www.unix.digital.com/faqs/publications/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/
   V50A_HTML/ARH95BTE/INDEX.HTM#INDEX_5_SEC

With best regards
Uwe

PS: But, having a user base of about 1500 accounts I've not seen
    remarkable delays during login if the default template has not been
    modified in the manner described above.

